// Title: HackTool - ADCSPwn Execution
// Sigma ID: cd8c163e-a19b-402e-bdd5-419ff5859f12
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Florian Roth (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2021-07-31 | Modified: 2023-02-04
// ATT&CK: collection, credential-access, T1557.001
// Description: Detects command line parameters used by ADCSPwn, a tool to escalate privileges in an active
//   directory network by coercing authenticate from machine accounts and relaying to the certificate
//   service
// False positives:
//   - Unlikely
// References:
//   - https://github.com/bats3c/ADCSPwn
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ccbb0369507f796db0b0ae6854c8a2be471b9d84/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_hktl_adcspwn.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ProcessCommandLine contains " --adcs " and ProcessCommandLine contains " --port "
